## What This Is

Not a paper collection. Not notes. Not a PDF graveyard.

This is a **reading engine + mapping log** that answers:

| Question | Location |
|----------|----------|
| What did we read? | `/papers/` |
| Why did it matter? | `/annotations/` |
| What did it connect to? | `/maps/` |
| What artifacts did it spawn? | `/artifacts/` |
| What's the narrative? | `/meta/reading-log.md` |

**Pipeline:**
```
Google Scholar → skim abstracts → pull 1-2 → annotate → integrate → spawn artifact
```

---

## Directory Structure

```
/fan-library
   /papers                    # Source documents by domain
      /cognition              # How brains work
      /ai                     # Machine learning, LLMs, agents
      /type-systems           # Java, formal verification, PLT
      /learning-theory        # Pedagogy, skill acquisition
      /java-spec              # JLS, CERT, Oracle docs

   /annotations               # Interpreted/digested papers
      2026-01-type-promotion-cube.md
      2026-01-numeric-precision.md

   /maps                      # Conceptual models, diagrams
      cube-model.md           # Rubik's cube abstraction
      type-lattice.md         # Java numeric hierarchy
      cli-journey.md          # Skill acquisition strata

   /artifacts                 # Things that got built
      /pseudocode
      /simulations
      /diagrams
      /experiments

   /meta                      # The narrative layer
      reading-log.md          # Rolling research journal
      glossary.md             # Terms that matter
      open-questions.md       # Unresolved threads
```

---

## Intake Protocol

Every paper/source gets processed through this template:

```markdown
# Paper: [Title]

**Authors:** 
**Year:** 
**Link:** 
**Domain:** 

## 1. Why I pulled this
(what question was I trying to answer)

## 2. Core claims (plain English)
- 
- 
- 

## 3. Mechanisms / models
(diagrams, equations, processes)

## 4. What this connects to
- Cube model:
- Type system:
- CLI journey:
- Learning theory:

## 5. Frictions / doubts
(what didn't fit, what smelled wrong)

## 6. Artifacts spawned
- pseudocode:
- diagram:
- experiment:
- code:

## 7. One-sentence compression
(if I lost everything else, this survives)
```

---

## Integration Rules

A paper stays **unintegrated** until it does at least ONE of:
- [ ] Modifies a model doc
- [ ] Adds a glossary term
- [ ] Spawns pseudocode
- [ ] Creates a diagram
- [ ] Changes a design assumption

No decorative PDFs. Everything earns its place.

---

## The Philosophy

> You are not collecting facts.
> You are building a personal research substrate.

This repo is:
- Part **lab notebook** (what happened)
- Part **design doc** (what we're building)
- Part **reading group** (what we learned)
- Part **cognitive OS spec** (how the brain works)

---

## Current Research Threads

### 🧊 Type Systems as Group Theory
- Java numeric promotion as directed lattice
- Rubik's cube move algebra as metaphor
- Widening = clockwise (implicit), Narrowing = counter-clockwise (explicit)
- Precision loss as "parity error" (looks safe, corrupts hidden state)

### 🧠 Learning as System Building
- ADHD/autism learning style: no memorization, only machine construction
- CLI journey as abstraction strata (byte → orchestration)
- Bloom's taxonomy as operator set

### 🔧 Externalized Cognition
- RAM-only brain requires external scaffolding
- Notes → systems → artifacts pipeline
- "If I can't build a machine for it, I can't remember it"

